            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0496" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 16948/38–39.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Thompson
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-07-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1772.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the embassy’s No. 1657 and to
                    previous correspondence on the subject of the extradition of Juan de Dios
                    Rodriguez, I inclose herewith copy and translation of a note received today from
                    the foreign office, stating that the extradition of the above has been granted,
                    and that the accused has the right to resort to amparo within three days.</p>
                <p>I advised the department of the above in my telegram of to-day.</p>
                <p>In accordance with the department’s instruction No. 655, of March 30th, Sheriff
                    J. M. Riggan, at Pearsall, Tex., will be advised when the prisoner is ready for
                    delivery to him.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. E. Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d383-a1.xml" xpointer="d383-a1"/>
            </div>
